00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:45.000
The investment banking division

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:46.520
is basically corporate advisory.

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:48.740
What individuals do in the
investment banking division

00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:50.370
is help companies raise money,

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:52.510
whether it's through equity,

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:54.220
issuing equity or issuing debt.

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:56.260
They help companies
restructure their business,

00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:58.900
so they look at the company's
equity to debt ratio

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:01.870
and assess if a company can
be organized in a better way

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:03.950
in order to function more efficiently

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.130
and increase shareholder value.

00:03:06.130 --> 00:03:09.030
And they help companies
merge or take over.

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:10.550
So corporate advisory in essence

00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:12.170
focuses on all of these areas.

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:14.240
When you go into the
investment banking division

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:15.150
as a junior,

00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:18.290
you are going to be heavily
focused on building models,

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:20.720
financial models and
valuation models on Excel,

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:24.370
and working on presentation
skills on Microsoft PowerPoint.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:26.730
These are the two tools
that you're gonna be using

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:27.563
for the most part

00:03:27.563 --> 00:03:30.160
in your first few years in the
investment banking division.

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:32.200
And so, naturally you
bring a lot of that over

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:34.900
from management consulting
to investment banking

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:36.250
because you do a lot of that

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:37.990
in the world of consulting anyways.

00:03:37.990 --> 00:03:39.950
The hours in the
investment banking division

00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:41.800
are the longest in the industry.

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:43.500
You would get in at like nine AM

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:46.000
and then you would leave
in your first few years,

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:47.620
midnight, one AM, two AM.

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:49.060
It's very, very long,

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:49.980
but as a result,

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:52.090
you get compensated with large bonuses

00:03:52.090 --> 00:03:53.130
at the end of the year.

00:03:53.130 --> 00:03:54.770
And so, if that's something
you're interested in,

00:03:54.770 --> 00:03:56.200
it's something worth looking at.

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:58.770
I've done quite a few videos
on the work-life balance,

00:03:58.770 --> 00:03:59.980
salaries, all of that,

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:00.813
those are on my channel,

00:04:00.813 --> 00:04:02.370
you can check those
out in your spare time.

00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:04.500
Then we've got the sales
and trading division.

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:08.990
This is the markets aspect or
area of the investment bank.

00:04:08.990 --> 00:04:11.290
This is where you see
traders on the trading floor

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:13.210
glued into the financial markets.

00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:15.060
They are basically creating markets

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:18.060
for clients who want to buy
or sell financial securities

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:21.050
and connecting them with
other clients or individuals

00:04:21.050 --> 00:04:23.440
who want to buy and sell
financial securities.

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:24.810
The traders are on the trading floor,

00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:26.510
there's salespeople on the trading floor,

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:28.200
there's researchers on the trading floor.

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:30.230
All of these people are
coming up with ideas,

00:04:30.230 --> 00:04:33.680
executing ideas in order
to make a small commission

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:36.480
of the large sums of money
that the clients are trading.

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:37.610
So if you're interested

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:39.800
in getting stuck into
the financial markets,

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:42.820
whether that be as a
salesperson or a trader,

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:44.730
then this might be something
that you're interested in.

00:04:44.730 --> 00:04:46.210
Typically you would get in really early

00:04:46.210 --> 00:04:47.330
before the markets open,

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:48.530
so six or seven AM,

00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:50.800
and then you would leave at
like five, six, seven PM.

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:53.350
And then you've got asset
management and private banking.

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:55.500
These areas basically manage money

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:57.900
over a longterm horizon for their clients.

00:04:57.900 --> 00:04:58.950
The key difference is

00:04:58.950 --> 00:05:01.630
in private banking or
private wealth management

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:03.810
your clients are high
net worth individuals.

00:05:03.810 --> 00:05:04.770
So rich people,

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:06.650
celebrities, footballers, etc.

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:08.160
And then in asset management,

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:10.170
your clients are government organizations,

00:05:10.170 --> 00:05:12.120
local authorities, insurance companies,

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:15.120
pension schemes, sovereign
wealth funds, etc., etc.

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:16.230
So large corporations

00:05:16.230 --> 00:05:18.330
versus individuals and family offices.

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:20.000
In asset management and private banking,

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.430
you can be a salesperson

00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:22.900
where you're managing client relationships

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:24.300
or you can be a product person,

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:25.420
an investment professional,

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:26.253
getting the money in

00:05:26.253 --> 00:05:28.070
and investing it into
the financial markets.

00:05:28.070 --> 00:05:28.970
There are a lot of people

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:30.410
who come from management consulting

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:32.830
that break into asset
management or investment banking

00:05:32.830 --> 00:05:34.230
as salespeople, for example,

00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:36.040
because they have those qualities

00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:38.220
that allow them to build
client relationships.

00:05:38.220 --> 00:05:39.420
They have interpersonal skills,

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:40.550
they're good communicators,

00:05:40.550 --> 00:05:41.610
they're good team workers,

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:42.500
so on and so forth.

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:45.270
Key skills that are very
similar, PowerPoint presentation.

00:05:45.270 --> 00:05:46.850
You use a lot in consulting,

00:05:46.850 --> 00:05:48.840
you use a lot in banking, why?

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:51.370
Because a lot of the work that a bank does

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:54.660
or a consulting firm does is
pitch to clients on PowerPoint.

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:57.380
If you are very good at
Microsoft PowerPoint,

00:05:57.380 --> 00:05:59.940
you will be able to work
faster, more efficiently,

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:02.120
and just impress your
seniors a lot easier.

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:03.730
And so, that's one key similarity

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:04.870
between the two industries.

00:06:04.870 --> 00:06:06.170
Another one is Excel,

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:08.120
I'm not too sure how
much you guys use Excel

00:06:08.120 --> 00:06:09.470
in management consulting.

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:10.560
I'm sure you use it quite a bit,

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:13.240
but it's heavily used in
investment banking division

00:06:13.240 --> 00:06:14.420
and on the trading floor.

00:06:14.420 --> 00:06:16.280
And so, if you are good on Excel,

00:06:16.280 --> 00:06:17.220
then that will be a bonus.

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:18.053
In both worlds,

00:06:18.053 --> 00:06:20.380
you go and manage client relationships,

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:23.380
you are pitching your ideas
and solutions to the clients,

00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:24.680
and you're trying to help them, right?

00:06:24.680 --> 00:06:25.860
And then in the process,

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:27.690
you take a fee for that service.

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:30.110
However, if you wanna move
from management consulting

00:06:30.110 --> 00:06:32.310
to investment banking specifically,

00:06:32.310 --> 00:06:34.960
it's important to understand
that in investment banking,

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:38.340
you need a good understanding
of accounting principles.

00:06:38.340 --> 00:06:39.980
You need to be able to look

00:06:39.980 --> 00:06:42.600
into the inner workings of a company

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:44.200
by reading its financial statements

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:46.770
and have an understanding
of what it all means.

00:06:46.770 --> 00:06:48.180
That's what the investment bank does,

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:49.460
it takes all of that information

00:06:49.460 --> 00:06:50.850
and puts it into the Excel models.

00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:52.840
And then it predicts or estimates

00:06:52.840 --> 00:06:54.470
the future performance of that company

00:06:54.470 --> 00:06:55.860
in different scenarios.

00:06:55.860 --> 00:06:56.930
In management consulting,

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:58.370
I'm not sure how much of that you do,

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:00.160
but if you're considering
breaking into banking,

00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:02.560
it's always good to have
some background knowledge

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:05.700
in accounting principles and
financial statement analysis.

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:06.880
If you wanna make the transition

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:08.970
from management consulting to banking,

00:07:08.970 --> 00:07:10.130
whether it's in asset management,

00:07:10.130 --> 00:07:10.963
sales and trading,

00:07:10.963 --> 00:07:13.140
private banking or the
investment banking division,

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:13.973
